id: pm-11phn1
title: "GH-817: machine-readable flag contracts need semantic invocation metadata and stdin capability"
description: "pm contracts command_flags currently exposes flag names without descriptions, value types, required/repeatable semantics, or accepts_stdin, forcing agents back to human help and hiding safe streaming paths for body-sized inputs."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:contracts","area:sdk",context-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-29T22:22:14.499Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T22:22:14.499Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: command_flags entries expose descriptions value types required repeatable and accepts_stdin from one canonical declaration; body and description stdin support is documented consistently in help and contracts; CLI SDK MCP and generated schemas remain parity-checked; compact contract projections remain bounded and measured; installed-consumer acceptance proves agents can discover and use stdin without scraping help
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make machine contracts sufficient to invoke every declared flag safely
value: Agents select streaming and typed invocation paths without spending context on help prose or risking argv limits
impact: Enriches the universal command contract for core and extension-provided flags
why_now: GH-817 demonstrates that the recommended discovery path cannot explain how to call its own flags
